    explanation: `A **ground transition** is any movement from one recognised position to another: guard to half guard, side control to mount, mount to back control, and so on. Ground fighting is rarely a single static hold from start to finish; it is a sequence of transitions, some completed cleanly, many contested and only partially successful, that together decide where a ground exchange ends up.`,
