    howItWorks: `A fighter pinning an opponent against the cage generally drives their hips into the opponent's body and uses their overall weight, not only their arms, to remove the space an opponent would need to circle away or reset the clinch. Grips such as underhooks or collar ties support this, but the pin itself is largely a matter of body positioning and weight distribution rather than grip strength alone.`,
